# Optional reverse proxy for deck-harness-server. NOT required to run the
# harness — deck-harness-server already serves both /api/* and the built
# client-deck SPA itself on its own PORT (see deck-harness-server/.env,
# default 4100). Use this only if/when you want:
#
#   - a stable port-80 LAN hostname instead of remembering :4100
#   - to front multiple harnesses behind one Caddy instance on the same box
#     later, per docs/arch/pi-harness.md's "Suggested structure"
#
# Intentionally LAN-only, unlike track-web's Caddyfile: no public DNS record,
# no automatic Let's Encrypt. This harness is meant to run somewhere with no
# exposure to the public internet (e.g. a NUC on the home LAN) — see
# docs/arch/pi-harness.md's security notes on why (the bash/write/edit tool
# surface is a much bigger blast radius than anything track-web exposes
# publicly). Replace deck.local with a hostname you've pointed at this box
# (router DNS, /etc/hosts, mDNS/avahi) or just proxy by IP.
#
# Formatting: tabs not spaces. Run `caddy fmt --overwrite Caddyfile` after edits.

deck.local {
	reverse_proxy localhost:4100
}
